        "original_id": "d0821de1-1f0b-5f48-b91d-ea693fe7020b",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Thomas Rickman, Sissy Spacek, Loretta Lynn, Tommy Lee Jones, Martha Plimpton, Tony Frank\n- Films: Coal Miner's Daughter, Hooper, Tuesdays with Morrie, Truman, The River Rat, Extreme Prejudice, Talk Radio, Born on the Fourth of July, Riverbend, Rush, Lone Star\n- Roles: film director, screenwriter, actor, Best Actress\n\nFacts:\n- Thomas Rickman, sometimes credited as Tom Rickman, is an American film director and screenwriter.\n- Thomas Rickman is known for the films Coal Miner's Daughter, Hooper, Tuesdays with Morrie, and Truman.\n- In 1980, Coal Miner's Daughter starred Sissy Spacek as Loretta Lynn.\n- Sissy Spacek won the Academy Award for Best Actress for her role as Loretta Lynn in Coal Miner's Daughter.\n- In 1984, The River Rat was released as an independent family film directed by Thomas Rickman.\n- The River Rat starred Tommy Lee Jones and Martha Plimpton.\n- Tony Frank acted in The River Rat in 1984, Extreme Prejudice in 1987, Talk Radio in 1988, Born on the Fourth of July in 1989, Riverbend in 1989, Rush in 1991, and Lone Star in 1996.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
